As Jouni described in his presentation at the Linux Wireless summit, all 
of the outstanding amendments (802.11k, 802.11n, 802.11r, ...) were 
rolled up into IEEE 802.11-2012.  The document is available for free 
download from IEEE at:

	http://standards.ieee.org/getieee802/download/802.11-2012.pdf

Additionally, 802.11aa and 802.11ae were published earlier this year. 
802.11ae is available for free download from IEEE at:

	http://standards.ieee.org/getieee802/download/802.11ae-2012.pdf

802.11aa is not yet available for free download, but should be in a 
couple months.

